  "verdict": "4 of 4 tier 3 pairs have a panel sequence identical to UniProt, an offset read from UniProt's own Signal or Propeptide boundary, and the correct wild-type residue at mature+offset: P00588, P04977, P0DPI1, P02879. Tier 3 is NOT dropped. \u26a0\ufe0f The identity check pins the offset on its own for only 1 of 4 (P04977), because a single substitution is one constraint and leaves about six admissible offsets by chance; the other three rest on the UniProt feature boundary, which is independent of the identity check but is a single source. Only 2 of 4 carry a UniProt Mutagenesis phenotype meeting the tier 2 loss-of-function rule (P04977, P0DPI1). The ricin row does not survive as written: its active-site substitution carries no UniProt Mutagenesis annotation at all, so there is no phenotype text to meet the tier 2 rule, and the only loss-of-function variants the entry annotates are vascular-leak-syndrome motif residues, not active-site ones."
